{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 17, :comments ["<b>Harass the Midianites.</b> After He gave the good reward to the righteous, He commanded to take vengeance upon the wicked, and said to him: ״צרור את המדינים״ — but not the Moabites, on account of Ruth the Moabitess, from whom David was destined to emerge." "<b>By way of the Midrash.</b> ״צרור את המדינים״ — ״for they are enemies (צוררים) to you.״ From this the Sages said: If one comes to kill you, rise early to kill him."], :book :numbers, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 25, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:36:07.729726105Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}